<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="research-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Br J Cancer</journal-id><journal-title>British Journal of Cancer</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0007-0920</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1532-1827</issn></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">764844</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2024837</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Research Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Reduced lethality in mice receiving a combined dose of cyclophosphamide and busulphan.</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Millar</surname><given-names>J. L.</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Hudspith</surname><given-names>B. N.</given-names></name></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Blackett</surname><given-names>N. M.</given-names></name></contrib></contrib-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><month>8</month><year>1975</year></pub-date><volume>32</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>193</fpage><lpage>198</lpage><abstract><p>Animals treated with a sufficiently high dose of busulphan die about 14 days later from bone marrow failure. A single, appropriately timed injection of cyclophosphamide can save these mice. The nature of this protection is shown to be the cyclophosphamide induced elaboration of a humoral factor which stimulates haemopoietic recovery.</p></abstract></article-meta></front><body><supplementary-material content-type="scanned-pages"><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00317-0049.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="193" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00317-0050.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="194" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00317-0051.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="195" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00317-0052.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="196" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00317-0053.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="197" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00317-0054.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="198" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/></supplementary-material></body></article>